# Discriminating pair, HALF 2 of 2: a program diverted to the tree-walk
# interpreter by a WHOLE-MODULE gate, which then runs perfectly and prints a
# perfectly ordinary result.
#
# The trigger is a REAL dependency: the `use std.io.window_winit...` import
# below. `exec_core.rs`'s `interpreter_preference_reason` parses the entry
# file's import declarations and diverts the module before the JIT is ever
# attempted when -- and only when -- a declaration actually names the
# `window_winit` module path. Merely MENTIONING the token in a comment or
# string literal no longer diverts; that substring gate was
# doc/08_tracking/bug/seed_window_winit_substring_lane_gate_2026-11-26.md.
# There is no per-function split on this path, and nothing here calls
# graphics.
#
# This is the exact shape that made engine A/B claims unfalsifiable: the run
# SUCCEEDS, exits 0, and its stdout is indistinguishable from a JIT run. Only
# the receipt separates them. Its receipt must read
# `engine=interpreter demoted=yes reason=jit-unsafe-graphics ...`.
use std.io.window_winit.{winit_loop_new}
fn main() -> i64:
    print "ok"
    0
